  "description": "SAPLED crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C83 H71 Dy3 N8 Ni4 O23,3(C2 H3 N1),2(C1 H4 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 3 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.146-3.938 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.74-131.39°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy3Ni4(L)6(OH)4(CH3OH)3(CH3CN)(NO3)(H2O)]·(CH3CN)3(CH3OH)2(H2O)2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Dy(III), Ni(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
